WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:11.480
Sarah Chen (PM): Okay, let's start. Two things for the enterprise launch on December 1st: account recovery and order history.

2
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:21.300
Sarah Chen (PM): Support says about forty percent of tickets are users who are locked out. We need self-service password reset by email.

3
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:30.900
Omar Haddad (Eng): Agreed. The reset link should expire after thirty minutes and only work once. And we should not reveal whether an email is registered.

4
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:39.750
Priya Nair (Security): From the security side, lock the account for fifteen minutes after five failed login attempts, and email the user when that happens.

5
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.600
Omar Haddad (Eng): Lockout and reset can share the same email service. Delivery should take under a minute.

6
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:58.300
Sarah Chen (PM): Second topic. Enterprise customers want to see their order history for the last twelve months and download it as CSV for their accounting.

7
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:07.200
Omar Haddad (Eng): The order list should be paginated, twenty-five per page, and filterable by date range and status.

8
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:15.400
Sarah Chen (PM): The CSV needs order number, date, items, total and status. Must have for launch.

9
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:23.800
Priya Nair (Security): Users must only ever see their own orders. Admins of an enterprise account can see all orders for that account.

10
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:31.200
Omar Haddad (Eng): One open thing: do enterprise customers need single sign-on for launch? Nobody has decided that yet.

11
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:38.600
Sarah Chen (PM): Let's not commit to SSO for December. Dark mode came up again too, but that's a nice-to-have for later.

12
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.000
Sarah Chen (PM): Great, that's it. Thanks everyone.
